From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:33:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi: a64: OHCI1's clock is parented on OHCI0's

Linux models this - ccu-sun50i-a64.c gives usb_ohci1_clk the parent
"usb-ohci0", while usb_ohci0_clk hangs off osc12M - but u-boot declared
the two as independent gates in the same register.

The difference only shows once ohci0 is disabled in the device tree.
Nothing then claims BIT(16), so OHCI1 comes up with its own gate set and
its upstream 12MHz source still gated, and "usb reset" hangs the board
hard: the console stops after "resetting USB..." and only a power cycle
recovers it. Verified on an A8 by clearing BIT(16) by hand at the u-boot
prompt - it reproduces exactly, and with this patch the same DT change
boots normally and takes ~1.1s off every usb reset.

.bit is a mask and sunxi_set_gate ORs it in, so claiming both bits is
enough. Note this is not a general parent implementation: disabling
OHCI1 now also gates OHCI0. Harmless here (they go down together in
usb_stop) but worth knowing before reusing it.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a64.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi/clk_a64.c
@@ -55,7 +55,15 @@
 	[CLK_USB_HSIC]		= GATE(0x0cc, BIT(10)),
 	[CLK_USB_HSIC_12M]	= GATE(0x0cc, BIT(11)),
 	[CLK_USB_OHCI0]		= GATE(0x0cc, BIT(16)),
-	[CLK_USB_OHCI1]		= GATE(0x0cc, BIT(17)),
+	/*
+	 * OHCI1's clock is parented on OHCI0's, not on osc12M directly -
+	 * linux models this (ccu-sun50i-a64.c: usb_ohci1_clk parent is
+	 * "usb-ohci0"), u-boot did not. With ohci0 disabled in the DT nothing
+	 * claims BIT(16), so OHCI1 came up with its own gate set and its
+	 * upstream 12MHz source dead, and "usb reset" hung the board hard.
+	 * .bit is a mask and sunxi_set_gate ORs it in, so claim both.
+	 */
+	[CLK_USB_OHCI1]		= GATE(0x0cc, BIT(17) | BIT(16)),
 
 	[CLK_DE]		= GATE(0x104, BIT(31)),
 	[CLK_TCON0]		= GATE(0x118, BIT(31)),
